# {{DIST}}

{{DESCRIPTION}}

{{SKILL_COUNT}} [Agent Skills](https://agentskills.io) for [Union.ai](https://www.union.ai),
packaged for every agent harness — plus two MCP servers (`flyte-docs`, `flyte-cluster`) for
harnesses that read the bundled `.mcp.json`.

The skills walk an agent and a human through Union.ai
[self-serve setup](https://www.union.ai/docs/v2/union/deployment/self-serve/) together:
provisioning AWS, connecting a cluster, running workflows, and debugging a data plane that
will not come up. Every command that creates a cloud resource is an explicit approval gate,
and every value that has to cross between the terminal and the Union.ai UI is marked as a
hand-off.

## Install

<!-- pypi-only:start -->
```bash
uvx {{DIST}} install
```

Or `pip install {{DIST}}` and then `{{DIST}} install`.
<!-- pypi-only:end -->
<!-- npm-only:start -->
### As a Claude Code plugin (npm source)

Add an entry to your marketplace's `marketplace.json`:

```json
{
  "name": "union",
  "source": { "source": "npm", "package": "{{DIST}}", "version": "^{{VERSION}}" }
}
```

Claude Code runs `npm install` and reads `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` from the package root.

### As a CLI that copies skills into your harness

```bash
npx {{DIST}} install
```
<!-- npm-only:end -->

The CLI auto-detects which harnesses are set up on the machine and copies the skills into
each one's skills directory:

| `--target` | User-level directory | Project-level (`--project`) | Read by |
|---|---|---|---|
| `agents` | `~/.agents/skills/` | `.agents/skills/` | Codex, Hermes (project), any harness following the convention |
| `claude` | `~/.claude/skills/` | `.claude/skills/` | Claude Code |
| `hermes` | `~/.hermes/skills/` | `.hermes/skills/` | Hermes |
| `opencode` | `~/.config/opencode/skills/` | `.opencode/skills/` | opencode |
| `pi` | `~/.pi/agent/skills/` | — | pi |

```bash
{{DIST}} install --target claude --target hermes  # pick harnesses explicitly
{{DIST}} install --target agents                  # the cross-harness standard location
{{DIST}} install --dir ./somewhere/skills         # arbitrary directory
{{DIST}} install --project                        # this repo only
{{DIST}} install --dry-run                        # show what would change
{{DIST}} uninstall                                # remove them again
{{DIST}} list                                     # list bundled skills
{{DIST}} path                                     # print the bundled plugin root
```

## MCP servers

`{{DIST}} install` writes skills only. `{{DIST}} mcp install` adds the two bundled MCP
servers as well, by driving `claude mcp add-json` / `codex mcp add` rather than editing
config files — so it needs one of those CLIs on your PATH:

```bash
{{DIST}} mcp list                     # what would be added
{{DIST}} mcp install --dry-run        # print the commands, change nothing
{{DIST}} mcp install                  # add them
{{DIST}} mcp uninstall                # remove them again
```

These are tools the agent can call, not inert markdown: `flyte-docs` sends search queries to
a Union-operated endpoint, and `flyte-cluster` gets control-plane access to your Union.ai
organization (which also needs `uv` and a login). Union.ai uses the same `flyte` SDK and CLI
as open-source Flyte, which is why the servers carry those names.

Harnesses that consume the whole plugin (Claude Code, Codex) pick the servers up from
`.mcp.json` automatically and need none of this.

## Native install paths

If you'd rather install from git than from a registry, the repo is a plugin marketplace in
its own right:

```
/plugin marketplace add unionai-oss/union-skills
/plugin install union@union-skills
```

See [the repository README]({{REPO_URL}}#readme) for Codex, Hermes, opencode and pi
instructions, the full skill list, and MCP server details.

